# Complex tasks → Sonnet 4.6 thinking

When the **user states the task is complex** (or clearly equivalent: complicated, large scope, multi-step architecture, needs deep reasoning), **use that heavier model for agent work**.

## Subagents (Task tool)

- For any **Task** / subagent invocation driven by that kind of request, set **`model` to `claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking`** (Claude Sonnet 4.6 with extended thinking).
- Use an appropriate **`subagent_type`** (`generalPurpose`, `explore`, `shell`, etc.) for the job; the model flag is what must be Sonnet 4.6 thinking here.

## Main chat

- If the primary work stays in the **current** chat (no Task), prefer the **Sonnet 4.6 Thinking** (or equivalent) model in the composer when the user has signaled complexity—**do not** default to a lighter model for that message thread when they asked for the deep-reasoning tier.

Only use this when the user (or the combined thread context) **explicitly frames the work as complex** or obviously needs long-horizon reasoning; do not escalate routine edits.
